From 12fbea16f2655f6cd54510bb5f10856160eb5ee4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:53:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] board: amlogic: add the S905X5 BL201 reference board

Add support for the Amlogic S905X5 (S6) BL201 reference board, with the
board device tree from the Linux tree used with it.

Supported: console on UART B (921600 baud), SD card, eMMC (high speed
SDR, the MMC driver has no HS200/HS400 tuning), Gigabit Ethernet on
RGMII, I2C, GPIOs and the fixed regulators.

As on the Khadas VIM4, the Ethernet MAC address is derived from the SoC
serial number and also set on the OS MAC node when the OS device tree
has no "ethernet0" alias.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
